<title>GERMANY: German union boss- Kohl legacy &quot;social division&quot;.</title>
<headline>German union boss- Kohl legacy &quot;social division&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Klaus Zwickel, head of the German IG Metall metalworkers and engineering trade union, said on Wednesday that Chancellor Helmut Kohl would be remembered as a proponent of social division.</p>
<p>&quot;Helmut Kohl wanted to go down in history as the Chancellor of national unification. Helmut Kohl will leave the political stage as the Chancellor of social division,&quot; Zwickel said on the second day of a union-organised jobs conference.</p>
<p>He said Kohl represented what he called neo-conservative politics in which international competitiveness took priority and jobs were a side-product.</p>
<p>Zwickel said that the creation and sharing of work should be the highest priority in a society.</p>
<p>--Mark John, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
